      "body": "### Project URL\n\nhttps://github.com/Blue-B/WhisperSubTranslate\n\n### Category\n\nJS\n\n### Project Title\n\nA desktop app that turns local videos into SRT subtitles and translates them offline\n\n### Project Description\n\nWhisperSubTranslate is a Windows desktop app for creating subtitles from video audio. It uses whisper.cpp for speech-to-text, supports local Hy-MT2 translation without API keys, and can also use DeepL, OpenAI, Gemini, or MyMemory.\n\n### Highlights\n\nThe main idea is local-first subtitle work: video files do not need to be uploaded, and Python setup is not required. It ships as a portable Electron app, downloads speech models on demand, and includes large-v2 Sync / Sync Lite for videos where normal Whisper timestamps drift, especially Japanese, Korean, and Chinese content.\n\n### Example Code\n\n```bash\n# No code is required for normal users.\n# Download the Windows portable archive and run WhisperSubTranslate.exe.\n```\n\n### Screenshots or Demo Videos\n\n![WhisperSubTranslate main UI](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Blue-B/WhisperSubTranslate/main/assets/hero/hero.png)\n\n![Hy-MT2 translation benchmark](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Blue-B/WhisperSubTranslate/main/assets/hy-mt2-benchmark.zh.png)\n",
